{"availability":"available","full":"dereuromark/cakephp-queue","name":"cakephp-queue","description":"Queue plugin for CakePHP - simple, pure PHP and without dependencies.","category":"Other","language":"PHP","stars":308,"forks":135,"created":"2011-10-09T17:09:44Z","updated":"2026-10-11T23:07:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://dereuromark.github.io/cakephp-queue/","topics":["asynchronous","background-jobs","cakephp","cakephp-plugin","cronjob","php","queue"],"demo":"https://sandbox.dereuromark.de/sandbox/queue-examples","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T06:27:45.642Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T06:27:45.642Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T06:27:45.642Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:38.153Z","stars":308,"forks":135},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:27:45.642Z","stars":308,"forks":135}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This branch is for use with CakePHP 5.1+. For details see version map.","Deferred execution makes sense (especially in PHP) when your page wants to execute tasks, which are not directly related to rendering the current page. For instance, in a BBS-type system, a new users post might require the creation of multiple personalized email messages, notifying other users of the new content. Creating and sending these emails is completely irrelevant to the currently active user, and should not increase page response time. Another example would be downloading, extraction and/or analyzing an external file per request of the user. The regular solution to these problems…","The Queue plugin provides a simple method to create and run such non-user-interaction-critical tasks."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dereuromark/cakephp-queue/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"b26a6cbaa31a658d907ef74bb00ce1ae352afbbf6cfa3e302989c982505f3282","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:38.308Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:38.308Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"